PROJECT: OpenSiPM CsI(Tl)+SiPM gamma spectrometer. First electronics project; user has
electrical knowledge and CAD skills. Budget hard cap $200, current design ~$125-135.
Goals: counts/sec first, spectroscopy second, rough isotope ID nice-to-have. RadiaCode-style
but not accuracy-critical. Rule: design must be fully finished before buying anything.

REFERENCE: Open Gamma Detector (OGD) Rev 4.2 analog design (MAX5026 bias, OPA357 preamp,
peak-hold with BAT54 + 470 pF film C8, 2N7002 reset, TLV3201 comparator, Pico 2 ADC).
Do NOT mix with the OpenGammaKit BOM (different design: MAX1422 ADC, transformer, digital pots).

FINAL ARCHITECTURE: SiPM -> OPA357 preamp/shaper -> OPA357 peak-hold -> Pico 2 ADC.
Firmware threshold replaces the comparator: Pico polls the peak-hold (GP26), reads a few us
after a crossing, pulses the 2N7002 to reset. GP27 = raw preamp tap, GP28 = NTC.

BOM: CsI(Tl) 10x10x10 mm + reflector (~$48), onsemi MicroFC-60035-SMT-TR (~$21-28),
2x OPA357AIDBVR, adjustable >=35 V boost module + 2-stage RC filter on a header,
BAT54, 2N7002 + 100R, 10k NTC (next to SiPM) + 10k 0.1% + 100 nF, 2 ferrite beads, 0603
resistors/caps (OGD values; 470 pF film C8; >=50 V caps on the ~30 V node), 3 test pads,
plain Pico 2 (not W) on sockets, 2-layer PCB, silicone grease, black tape/Kapton, tin shield,
printed case. Power: USB for v1. Later: digital pots, Bluetooth, battery (+~$20).

KEY FACTS: SiPM breakdown ~24.2-24.7 V, operate ~27.5-29.6 V, NEVER above ~29.7 V.
SiPM gain drifts -0.8%/C. CsI(Tl) emits ~540 nm (SiPM peaks ~420 nm) with ~1 us decay, so
sample delay needs retuning vs the NaI-tuned OGD firmware. Don't use a BAT54 as the boost
rectifier (30 V rating). Startup: SiPM disconnected, set bias, verify with multimeter, power
down, connect SiPM, recheck.

EXPECTATIONS (my estimates, unverified): resolution ~10-14% at 662 keV, ~8-10% best case;
~1 cm3 crystal = slow stats; no alpha/beta discrimination; no temperature compensation in
hardware (firmware correction via NTC + K-40 reference peak). Test sources: KCl salt (K-40
1461 keV), uranium glass (Bi-214 609 keV), smoke detector Am-241 59.5 keV (keep sealed).

ISOTOPE ID PLAN: 2-point keV calibration (Am-241 + K-40), smooth, peak-find, match against
a small library (K-40, Cs-137, Co-60, Am-241, Ba-133, Na-22, Bi-214, Tl-208) with
energy-scaled tolerance, score by fraction of lines matched, subtract a background run.

OPEN ITEMS: LTspice sim of preamp + peak-hold with onsemi's SiPM model; confirm cap voltage
ratings on the ~30 V node; verify Pico 2 GPIO23 power-mode pin; plan crystal-over-SiPM
mounting (10x10 crystal, 7x7 SiPM package); write firmware trigger loop and a synthetic
test spectrum. Prices and the PDE of the SiPM at 540 nm are not verified.
